and global geopolitical noise, with markets pricing in limited near-term easing. Nuclear power

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:31.520
buildouts are emerging as a sector leader this week as countries accelerate reactor plans through

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:39.940
2040. Our matched window alpha sits at negative 0.89%, which tells us the recent setups have not

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:46.300
kept pace with the NASDAQ during overlapping holding periods. That nuclear demand signal is

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:52.040
exactly why we are opening today's strategy spotlight on how to invest in the supply chain rather

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:58.100
than the utilities themselves. Nuclear supply chain investing focuses on companies that provide

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:03.980
uranium, specialized mining inputs, or reactor components rather than pure power utilities.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:10.420
Today's combination of global reactor commitments and Canada's federal target of 10 new units

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:16.760
by 2040 creates a multi-year demand signal that is independent of short-term oil moves.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:23.940
Investors can screen TSX listed names in the uranium and critical mineral space using free tools

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:31.080
such as the TMX market intelligence screener, filtering for market cap above $200 million and

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:37.280
positive free cash flow trends. The approach has historically delivered strongest results in the

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:45.400
early phases of multi-year CAPEX cycles, as seen in the 2005-2007 uranium bull market.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:52.180
That same period showed how volume spikes often confirmed the real start of sustained moves rather

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:59.420
than false starts. Pair any position with a same-day volume check above the 20-day average to avoid

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:06.540
low liquidity traps. Execution risk remains if project timelines slip, so the screen alone is

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:12.520
never enough without that liquidity filter. While we wait for clean volume signals and energy names,

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:18.100
let's examine a broader lesson that applies to every hot theme including today's AI stocks.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:25.280
Imagine you bought a high multiple semiconductor name last month after an AI infrastructure headline.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:31.600
Your order filled at the open, but the stock then dropped 8% on profit taking even though

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:39.620
fundamentals had not changed. The mechanism at work is identical to 1999 to 2000. Investors

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:45.840
priced in years of future growth in a single quarter, so any hint of slower CAPEX produced violent

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:53.840
repricing. The bid asked spread on many AI-related names widened from $5 to $0.25 in the first hour of

00:03:53.840 --> 00:04:00.460
trading on July 13 as volume spiked. What most retail investors miss is that the companies that

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:07.820
survived the .com bust already had real revenue and defensible cash flow models. While pets.com and

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:15.220
web van did not, AI stocks today sit in a middle ground, many report genuine revenue, yet valuations

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:21.740
still embed the same this time as different assumption. The biggest mistake is treating every AI

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:27.740
revenue beat as permanent. Instead, always demand three consecutive quarters of accelerating

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:33.860
free cash flow growth before adding to a position. That same discipline of waiting for confirmation

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:40.380
is why we are skipping a new trade today. This is a simulated trade for educational purposes only

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:47.360
with no real money involved. No new position is being initiated today. Oil price spike and nuclear

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:53.960
demand growth are both visible, yet no single ticker shows the three or more aligned factors of volume

00:04:53.960 --> 00:05:00.440
confirmation, technical setup and sector momentum required under the current regime. We are watching

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:06.680
for Canadian energy names to close above their 20-day volume average on the oil move, but none have

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:14.720
done so yet. The recent cold streak in matched window alpha at negative 0.89%, require stricter entry

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:20.740
criteria going forward. Skipping a trade when factors are not aligned demonstrates how to protect

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:27.120
the portfolio during low conviction periods and forces focus on only the highest quality setups.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:32.940
Listeners learn that patience is an active risk management decision, not in action.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:41.460
The explicit trigger we are monitoring is that volume spike plus RSI 14 moving above 45 from below.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:47.960
No newly closed trade since the last review means there is no new realized result to report today.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:53.940
The most recent practice investment has already been reviewed and current holdings remain open

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:59.620
pending their scheduled evaluation. This keeps the focus on the open position rather than

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:05.700
manufacturing a result that does not exist. When the next close arrives we will examine whether the

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:12.430
thesis played out and what moved the name. For now the absence of a new close reinforces the value

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:20.670
