00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:12.810
volume confirmation before any new simulated entry. This keeps the overall book focused on high

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:19.410
conviction names rather than forcing trades during mixed signals. Now, here's something that most

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:25.970
retail investors get wrong and it cost me money before I figured it out. You see a high multiple name

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:33.110
surge on an AI headline and jump in at the open only to watch it drop 8% the same day on profit

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:41.070
taking. The mechanism is the same as 1999 to 2000 when investors priced years of growth into one quarter

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:48.450
and any capex hint triggered violent repricing. The fix is simple, demand three consecutive quarters

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:54.850
of accelerating free cash flow growth before adding to the position. That single rule would have

00:10:54.850 --> 00:11:00.390
